========================================================================================================================
CATEGORY             DIAGNOSTIC TARGET           KUBECTL / TERMINAL COMMAND FOR OPERATIONS & TROUBLESHOOTING
========================================================================================================================
DEPLOY IMAGES        Run Standalone Pod          kubectl run test-pod --image=<registry>/<repo>/<image>:<tag>
DEPLOY IMAGES        Create Multi-Replica Deploy kubectl create deployment app-deploy --image=<image> --replicas=3
DEPLOY IMAGES        Update Container Image      kubectl set image deployment/app-deploy <container-name>=<new-image>:<tag>
DEPLOY IMAGES        Rollback Image Update       kubectl rollout undo deployment/app-deploy
DEPLOY IMAGES        Check Live Image Tag        kubectl get pods -o jsonpath='{.items[*].spec.containers[*].image}'
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRIVATE REPOS        Create Docker-Registry Secret kubectl create secret docker-registry regcred \
                                                   --docker-server=<registry-url> --docker-username=<user> \
                                                   --docker-password=<pass> --docker-email=<email>
PRIVATE REPOS        Verify Regcred Configuration  kubectl get secret regcred -o yaml
PRIVATE REPOS        Patch Default ServiceAccount  kubectl patch serviceaccount default -p '{"imagePullSecrets": [{"name": "regcred"}]}'
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
TROUBLESHOOTING      Track Image Pull Failures     kubectl get pods | grep -E "ImagePullBackOff|ErrImagePull"
TROUBLESHOOTING      Inspect Image Pull Event Logs kubectl describe pod <pod-name>
TROUBLESHOOTING      Check Node Disk Image Space   kubectl describe node <node-name> | grep -A 5 -i "Taints"
TROUBLESHOOTING      Force Immediate Image Pull    kubectl set env deployment/app-deploy REFRESH_DATE=$(date +%s)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NODE LEVEL (SSH)     List Cached Local Images      crictl images         <-- Run via SSH on the worker node
NODE LEVEL (SSH)     Manually Pull Missing Image   crictl pull <image>   <-- Run via SSH on the worker node
NODE LEVEL (SSH)     Inspect Container Engine Logs journalctl -u containerd -n 100 <-- Run via SSH on the worker node
========================================================================================================================
